const how={dashboard:'Cash is the latest available balance in each store’s checking and savings, from Plaid. Sales, operating income and labor % use the newest month QuickBooks has closed; open months are labeled and kept out of totals. Store totals exclude B&B and parent companies and do not eliminate intercompany activity.',banking:'Balances are the latest bank snapshots returned through Plaid, not live balances. Card spend is net posted spend from BILL, not the card balance or available credit. Owed amounts are current balances on connected loan and credit accounts and are never subtracted from cash. Payroll lives in Payroll.',books:'QuickBooks reported results. A month counts as closed when QuickBooks no longer marks it partial; that is not a completed accounting review. Totals add only stores that closed the month and exclude B&B and parent companies.',payroll:'Labor cost is Gusto employer cost (wages, employer taxes and benefits) with tips removed; tips are never labor cost. When I Work hours include exported published and unpublished shifts; they are planned hours, not attendance. Imports are snapshots, not automatic connections.',insurance:'Policies come from policy documents saved in each store. Fran reads dates and coverage types; it does not judge whether coverage is adequate.'}[view]||'Figures retain their source dates. Missing records are not zero. Evidence preparation is not lender approval.';
